berkeley-principles-1.md:1: argue/answered: S4: answered no, which keeps berkeley-principles-1.logic.r1, to: Suppose "sweetness appears various to different perceivers or at different stations while the object remains unaltered" is false. Is S4, "Again, it is proved that SWEETNESS is not really in the sapid thing, because the thing remaining unaltered the sweetness is changed into bitter, as in case of a fever or otherwise vitiated palate.", true then? [in 1 of 2 runs]
